WEBVTT

00:00.824 --> 00:01.801
A shared phone.

00:01.858 --> 00:03.892
Twenty minutes, three days a week.

00:03.949 --> 00:06.344
No tutor, no reliable internet.

00:06.413 --> 00:08.989
This is Maya — and there are millions like her.

00:14.648 --> 00:16.375
Bright students in underserved schools

00:16.415 --> 00:19.339
don't lack free material — they lack follow-through.

00:19.408 --> 00:22.861
Practice results, class notes, occasional tutoring:

00:22.893 --> 00:26.178
all fragmented. Every session starts from zero.

00:30.536 --> 00:32.282
A chatbot answers questions.

00:32.339 --> 00:33.713
An agent takes action.

00:33.769 --> 00:38.465
GitLearnOS turns one learner-owned Git repository into durable state —

00:38.505 --> 00:41.770
so any AI agent becomes a tutor that never forgets,

00:41.810 --> 00:43.148
and never locks you in.

00:48.436 --> 00:51.048
Real practice becomes an evidence-linked gap.

00:51.104 --> 00:54.305
The agent picks the smallest useful next question —

00:54.338 --> 00:55.555
not another worksheet.

00:55.612 --> 00:57.290
Every answer is preserved,

00:57.330 --> 00:59.858
every step is a reversible Git commit.

00:59.914 --> 01:02.478
Auditable. Undoable. Yours.

01:07.736 --> 01:08.629
Watch it work.

01:08.686 --> 01:10.949
Maya gives the agent her constraints.

01:11.005 --> 01:14.050
It reads her durable state — not the open web —

01:14.094 --> 01:16.526
and asks exactly one fresh question.

01:16.594 --> 01:18.365
She answers in her own words.

01:18.433 --> 01:20.845
The agent writes it all back, commits,

01:20.885 --> 01:22.571
and schedules the next check.

01:22.628 --> 01:24.403
And it refuses to claim mastery

01:24.443 --> 01:26.153
without delayed evidence.

01:26.222 --> 01:28.389
That's discipline a chatbot doesn't have.

01:53.236 --> 01:57.603
Text-first. No database, no server, nothing always-on.

01:57.659 --> 02:00.547
It works with the free materials schools already have,

02:00.580 --> 02:02.836
and with any agent the student can reach —

02:02.876 --> 02:07.362
ChatGPT, Claude, Codex, OpenCode — or none at all.

02:07.419 --> 02:09.393
The learner owns every byte.

02:15.836 --> 02:16.981
GitLearnOS.

02:17.038 --> 02:20.118
Learning happens anywhere — the state belongs to you.
